-- title:
--   Level raising at q ∣ N preserves corner components
-- statement:
--   Let $N$ and $q$ be non-zero naturals with $q$ prime and $q \mid N$, and let $h_1$, $h_q$ be witnesses of [`CohCarrier.LevelLE`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L330) from level $N$ with full unit subgroup to level $Nq$ with full unit subgroup, with degeneracy parameters $1$ and $q$ respectively (i.e. $N \mid Nq$, the parameter divides $(Nq)/N$, and the reduction condition on the unit subgroups, vacuous for $\top$). Let $S$ be a set of naturals and $\mathcal{O}$ a noetherian commutative local ring with residue field $k =$ `IsLocalRing.ResidueField 𝒪`. For a level $M$, [`CohCarrier.Gen M S`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L13) has generators $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell \notin S$, $\ell \nmid M$), $U_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell \mid M$) and $\langle d\rangle$ ($d \in (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$), acting on $H^1(M) := \operatorname{Hom}(\Gamma_H(M)^{\mathrm{ab}}, \mathcal{O})$ through [`CohCarrier.opFamily`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L91) (Hecke operators by corestriction along conjugated congruence subgroups, diamond operators by the $\Gamma_0$-action); $h_{\mathrm{comm}}$ and $h_{\mathrm{comm}}'$ assert that these operators commute at levels $N$ and $Nq$. Let $\bar\theta$, $\bar\theta'$ be $k$-valued functions on the generators at levels $N$, $Nq$, compatible in the sense that $\bar\theta'(T_\ell) = \bar\theta(T_\ell)$ for $\ell$ prime, $\ell \notin S$, $\ell \nmid Nq$; $\bar\theta'(U_\ell) = \bar\theta(U_\ell)$ for $\ell$ prime with $\ell \mid N$ and $\ell \neq q$; and $\bar\theta'(U_q) = 0$. Let $Sp$, resp. $Sp'$, be an [`IharaLemma.IdempotentSplitting`](def/IharaLemma_IdempotentSplitting.html#L7) of the $\mathcal{O}$-subalgebra generated by the operators at level $N$, resp. $Nq$ (a complete orthogonal family of idempotents $e_i$ together with maximal ideals $\mathfrak{m}_i$ exhausting the maximal spectrum, with $e_i \in \mathfrak{m}_j$ iff $i \neq j$), let $i_0$, $i_0'$ be indices, and let $\pi$, $\pi'$ be $\mathcal{O}$-algebra maps from the corner rings $e_{i_0} B e_{i_0}$, $e_{i_0'} B' e_{i_0'}$ to $k$ sending the corner image of each generator's operator to $\bar\theta$, resp. $\bar\theta'$, of that generator. Then for every $\varphi \in H^1(N)$ lying in the image of $e_{i_0}$, the class $\big(\iota_q^{*} \circ U_q - q\,\iota_1^{*}\big)\varphi$, with $\iota_d^{*} =$ [`CohCarrier.iDegL`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L401) for the respective `LevelLE` witness and $U_q =$ [`CohCarrier.heckeTL N ⊤ 𝒪 q`](def/CohCarrier_Inst.html#L23), lies in the image of $e_{i_0'}$ on $H^1(Nq)$.
--
--   This is the raising half of the level-raising step at a prime $q$ dividing the current level: the classical combination $\iota_q^{*}U_q - q\,\iota_1^{*}$ lands in the part of the cohomology at level $Nq$ on which $U_q$ acts by $0$, and the statement records that it respects the local components cut out by the chosen idempotents. It is the corner-stability input for the construction of a rung of the chain of levels, used in [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_isCornerRealization_and_rung_of_isCornerRealization_of_dvd_of_not_sq_dvd_of_not_cube_dvd`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_isCornerRealization_and_rung_of_isCornerRealization_of_dvd_of_not_sq_dvd_of_not_cube_dvd).
